IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 9.001 to 9.004: Search for Suitable Employment. Piece er1, layer 1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30
-- (../../registers/source-bundle/SOR-96-332.txt). Nothing here is verified against the official text. `src:N` is a line of that file.
-- Instrument: the Regulations, made for subsection 50(8) and paragraphs 18(1)(a) and 27(1)(a) to (c) of the Act (pieces
-- ei2 and ei1; the Act's rules that use these criteria are theirs, and take the BOOLEAN results below as inputs).
-- Both rules state criteria the claimant must meet, to be proved to the Commission; the judgment on the evidence is the
-- Commission's and is not encoded.

§ `Regulation 9.001 - reasonable and customary efforts`

-- src:136 | (b) the claimant’s efforts consist of
-- src:137 | (i) assessing employment opportunities,
-- src:138 | (ii) preparing a resumé or cover letter,
-- src:139 | (iii) registering for job search tools or with electronic job banks or employment agencies,
-- src:140 | (iv) attending job search workshops or job fairs,
-- src:141 | (v) networking,
-- src:142 | (vi) contacting prospective employers,
-- src:143 | (vii) submitting job applications,
-- src:144 | (viii) attending interviews, and
-- src:145 | (ix) undergoing evaluations of competencies; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 9.001(b) (src:136-145)
-- Plain gloss (paragraph (b) alone): the job search is made up of some of the nine listed kinds of activity: looking at
-- what jobs exist, preparing a resume or cover letter, signing up with job banks or agencies, going to job-search
-- workshops or fairs, networking, contacting employers, applying, going to interviews, and being assessed.
-- The list is joined by "and" ("... (viii) attending interviews, and (ix) undergoing evaluations of competencies"), but it
-- names kinds of effort and no claimant could be doing all nine at once; so it is read as: at least one of the nine
-- (fork F6 in NOTES.md). Turning the OR into AND is the one change the other reading would make.
GIVEN `assessing employment opportunities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `preparing a resume or cover letter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `registering for job search tools or with electronic job banks or employment agencies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `attending job search workshops or job fairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `networking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contacting prospective employers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `submitting job applications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `attending interviews` IS A BOOLEAN
      `undergoing evaluations of competencies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 9.001(b) the claimant's efforts consist of one or more of the listed kinds of effort` IF
       `assessing employment opportunities`
    OR `preparing a resume or cover letter`
    OR `registering for job search tools or with electronic job banks or employment agencies`
    OR `attending job search workshops or job fairs`
    OR `networking`
    OR `contacting prospective employers`
    OR `submitting job applications`
    OR `attending interviews`
    OR `undergoing evaluations of competencies`

-- src:134 | 9.001 For the purposes of subsection 50(8) of the Act, the criteria for determining whether the efforts that the claimant is making to obtain suitable employment constitute reasonable and customary efforts are the following:
-- src:135 | (a) the claimant’s efforts are sustained;
-- src:136 | (b) the claimant’s efforts consist of
-- src:146 | (c) the claimant’s efforts are directed toward obtaining suitable employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 9.001 (src:134) (src:135) (src:136) (src:146)
-- Plain gloss: the claimant's job search counts as reasonable and customary if it is sustained, is made up of the listed
-- kinds of effort, and is aimed at getting suitable employment. All three are required. Whether employment is "suitable"
-- is reg 9.002 below.
GIVEN `the claimant's efforts are sustained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's efforts consist of one or more of the listed kinds of effort` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's efforts are directed toward obtaining suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 9.001 the claimant's efforts to obtain suitable employment are reasonable and customary efforts` IF
        `the claimant's efforts are sustained`
    AND `the claimant's efforts consist of one or more of the listed kinds of effort`
    AND `the claimant's efforts are directed toward obtaining suitable employment`

§ `Regulation 9.002 - suitable employment`

-- src:149 | 9.002 (1) For the purposes of paragraphs 18(1)(a) and 27(1)(a) to (c) and subsection 50(8) of the Act, the criteria for determining what constitutes suitable employment are the following:
-- src:150 | (a) the claimant’s health and physical capabilities allow them to commute to the place of work and to perform the work;
-- src:151 | (b) the hours of work are not incompatible with the claimant’s family obligations or religious beliefs; and
-- src:152 | (c) the nature of the work is not contrary to the claimant’s moral convictions or religious beliefs.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 9.002(1) (src:149-152)
-- Plain gloss: work is suitable if the claimant's health and physical ability let them travel to it and do it, its hours
-- do not clash with their family duties or religious beliefs, and its nature is not against their moral convictions or
-- religious beliefs. "Not incompatible with the claimant's family obligations or religious beliefs" is read as not
-- incompatible with either (and likewise for paragraph (c)); the inputs are the clashes, so a TRUE answer is a clash.
GIVEN `the claimant's health and physical capabilities allow them to commute to the place of work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's health and physical capabilities allow them to perform the work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours of work are incompatible with the claimant's family obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours of work are incompatible with the claimant's religious beliefs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nature of the work is contrary to the claimant's moral convictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nature of the work is contrary to the claimant's religious beliefs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 9.002(1) suitable employment` IF
        `the claimant's health and physical capabilities allow them to commute to the place of work`
    AND `the claimant's health and physical capabilities allow them to perform the work`
    AND NOT (`the hours of work are incompatible with the claimant's family obligations`)
    AND NOT (`the hours of work are incompatible with the claimant's religious beliefs`)
    AND NOT (`the nature of the work is contrary to the claimant's moral convictions`)
    AND NOT (`the nature of the work is contrary to the claimant's religious beliefs`)

